From 71028253736ff298832a13dc081bb4eadc2a103e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bemly <bemly_@petalmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:55:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Sinytra patch 0001 (3/3): GeckoViewResponseController +
 docshell wrap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

C++ interception controller (parent process, mobile/android/components/
geckoview):
- nsINetworkInterceptController over the public necko contract: URIs
  matching a registered http(s) prefix filter claim the channel; the
  intercepted channel is answered by dispatching GeckoView:OnRequestResponse
  (C++-side, via the injected nsIGeckoViewEventDispatcher) to the app
  delegate (Group 1) and synthesizing the response with
  SynthesizeStatus/SynthesizeHeader/StartSynthesizedResponse — URL
  identity preserved by the internal redirect.
- App miss/error/body-cap refusals degrade honestly to ResetInterception
  (network proceeds untouched); everything else forwards to the wrapped
  ServiceWorkerInterceptController.
- Static SetFilters entry point (prefixes + dispatcher); inert until a
  caller registers filters.

nsDocShell wraps its ServiceWorkerInterceptController with this controller
on Android parent process. Build green end-to-end; device regression
(canary + 29-probe harness) unchanged with no filters registered.
---
