 dispatcher subject
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The observer-service subject was this.eventDispatcher — the
DispatcherDelegate JS wrapper (Messaging.sys.mjs), a pure JS object
with no QueryInterface. The C++ FilterPushObserver never fired at all
(no 'FilterPushObserver topic=' log — the notification could not be
marshaled, so the QI question never even arose).

Pass the NATIVE dispatcher instead: window.arguments[0] is
nsWindow::AndroidView, NS_IMPL_ISUPPORTS(..., nsIGeckoViewEvent-
Dispatcher, nsIGeckoViewView); QI it to nsIGeckoViewEventDispatcher.
The controller's later Dispatch to 'GeckoView:OnRequestResponse' uses
that same native dispatcher, which is what the design wanted.

After the fix the full chain lights up on device: FilterPushObserver
topic= -> filters pushed: 1 -> ShouldPrepare HIT -> ChannelIntercepted
-> OnSuccess.

Debug aids in this commit (downgrade before finalizing): dump() logs
in the JS case, process-type in the C++ registration log.
